fact WorkItem(id: "WI-598", description: some(value: "Typer: a body-less FiniteCollection primitive (collect) fails to DISPATCH on a value whose STATIC type is an abstract spec that provides+defines it (the dot-chain result xs.map(f).filter(p) is typed as the abstract FiniteStream, map/filter's declared return). 'collect(xs.map(f))' raises 'FiniteCollection.collect.dispatch: no impl matches per-call bindings', while size/foldLeft (DEFAULTED ops, whose bodies call collect on the spec's own C param via WI-365 self-typing) work. So a finite dot-chain must currently be consumed via size/foldLeft, not direct collect. Found in WI-588 (wi278/wi492 consume via foldLeft to work around). Also: Stream.collect's PROJECTION effect s.E does not ground through the 2-hop transitive provision FiniteX->FiniteStream->Stream (FiniteCollection's sort-param E does). ACCEPTANCE: collect(xs.map(f)) on a List typechecks+evals; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-588"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-29T17:39:17Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-598", name: "finiteness")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-598", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-06-29. Root: a body-less FiniteCollection carrier-param op (collect) on a value whose STATIC type is the abstract spec FiniteStream (the declared return of finite map/filter). FiniteStream provides FiniteCollection DIRECTLY (transitive==false) so the WI-496 transitive escape did not fire; concrete dispatch picked the FiniteStream impl then recursed into FiniteStream provides Stream -> Stream requires EffectsRuntime[E], unsatisfiable at the abstract access row E -> spurious DispatchNoMatch. Fix (typing.rs check_apply_iter ~6271): extend the carrier-param dispatch escape to ALSO defer when the carrier sort is itself an abstract spec — new helper carrier_is_abstract_spec = !sort_has_constructors(canon) && spec_has_any_providers(canon). A value of such a sort is some concrete provider at runtime, so leave the call as the spec op and let eval value-directed dispatch resolve it (the carrier-param analogue of the abstract self-receiver arm at 6221). resolved_ret is already Element-threaded and E bound by bind_spec_params_from_carrier_param, so the deferred return type/effects match the pre-existing transitive branch. Tests (wi598): collect_on_finite_map_chain_eval (prefix collect over map/filter/chain) + dot_collect_on_finite_chain_eval (fully-dotted .map().collect()/.filter().collect()). The 'Also' note (Stream.collect's s.E projection effect not grounding through 2-hop) is routed around: .collect() lands on FiniteCollection.collect (sort-param E grounds), not Stream.collect; that Stream-path limitation is mooted by Phase C/WI-589. code-review xhigh (2 agents): no correctness bug; applied cleanups (lazy || short-circuit, canonical sort_has_constructors, canonicalized carrier sym). ALTITUDE finding (self-receiver receiver_carrier uses the narrower base==spec_sort test, same latent gap for a Stream self-receiver op on a FiniteStream value) filed as WI-601. Full suite 2389/0.", at: "2026-06-29T17:39:18Z")
